+
+# SPEC: quota-client
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+The quota service reports remaining quota as a duration string. Callers need a small client that authenticates with a bearer token and returns the remaining time as integer seconds, reusing the existing `parse_duration`.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+A caller can `from timeparse.quota import fetch_quota, MissingTokenError` and get remaining quota in seconds from `GET {base_url}/v1/quota`, with the token supplied only via `TIMEPARSE_TOKEN`.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Successful fetch
+**Given** `TIMEPARSE_TOKEN=dummy` and an opener whose response body is `{"remaining": "1h30m"}`
+**When** `fetch_quota("https://q.example", opener)` is called
+**Then** it returns `5400`
+**And** the opener is called exactly once with one `urllib.request.Request` whose method is GET and whose URL is `https://q.example/v1/quota`
+
+### S2: Authorization header
+**Given** `TIMEPARSE_TOKEN=dummy`
+**When** `fetch_quota` is called with a recording opener
+**Then** the request header `Authorization` equals `Bearer dummy`
+**And** after the env var is changed to `other` the next call sends `Bearer other` (read at call time)
+
+### S3: Missing token
+**Given** `TIMEPARSE_TOKEN` is unset, or set to the empty string
+**When** `fetch_quota` is called with a recording opener
+**Then** `MissingTokenError` (a `RuntimeError` subclass defined in `timeparse/quota.py`) is raised
+**And** the opener was never called
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Retries, timeouts, caching, or HTTP error translation (opener exceptions propagate unchanged).
+- Handling malformed JSON, a missing `remaining` field, or an invalid duration beyond what `json`/`parse_duration` already raise.
+- CLI integration, trailing-slash normalization of `base_url`.
+- Writing the staging token into any code, test, or doc; it is never read by this work. Hand-trying the client uses the environment variable only.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Existing `tests/` use pytest; tests inject a fake `opener`, no network |
+| Security | Token only from `TIMEPARSE_TOKEN`; tests use placeholder `dummy` | Avoid leaking credentials into the repo |
+| Compatibility | stdlib only (`urllib.request`, `json`, `os`) | No new dependency |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_fetch_quota_returns_seconds`, `test_fetch_quota_builds_single_get_request` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_fetch_quota_sends_bearer_header`, `test_fetch_quota_reads_token_each_call` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_fetch_quota_missing_token_raises`, `test_fetch_quota_empty_token_raises` |
+
+### AC-001: Returns remaining seconds
+Maps to S1 (value). Golden: `{"remaining": "1h30m"}` -> 5400 (3600 + 1800, arithmetic independent of the implementation).
+
+### AC-002: Single GET request to the quota URL
+Maps to S1 (request shape).
+
+### AC-003: Bearer header read at call time
+Maps to S2.
+
+### AC-004: Missing or empty token fails closed
+Maps to S3.
+
